- Nested while loop means a while loop inside another while loop.
- The inner loop runs completely for every iteration of the outer loop.

l1=[10,20,30]
l2=[40,50,60]
i=0
while i < len(l1):
    j=0
    while j < len(l2):
        print(l1[i],l2[j])
        j=j+1
    print()
    i+=1

Output
-----
10 40
10 50
10 60

20 40
20 50
20 60

30 40
30 50
30 60

